https://your-store.example
ck_replace_with_your_consumer_key
cs_replace_with_your_consumer_secret
# Lines 1-3 are also what creates a batch's products on the website, instead
# of importing the CSV with WP All Import.
# Optional, lines 4 and 5: lets Alex Collect upload a replacement photo and
# set it on the product by itself, and upload a new product's front and back
# photos with it. Without them the products are still created - as drafts,
# waiting for their photos - and the app still saves and names every image
# for the media library.
# WooCommerce keys cannot touch the media library, so this needs a WordPress
# Application Password, not another WooCommerce key.
# Users > Profile > Application Passwords > Add New, then paste the name here:
wp_replace_with_your_wordpress_username
wp_replace_with_your_application_password
# Replace every example value with your own settings.
# WooCommerce > Settings > Advanced > REST API > Add key. Reading products
# needs Read-only; setting a product's photo, its stock, or creating a
# product needs Read/Write.
# Application Passwords need HTTPS, and WordPress 5.6 or newer.
# Save a private copy as woo-keys.txt; never publish that file.
